 "note": "Lunenburg High School: the 'SCHOOL STAFF' block (line 18) is headed by 'High School Principal' Frank A. Sambuceti and lists only high-school departments, and follows the end of the high school principal's report (lines 1-17, NEASC accreditation narrative, ignored). Line 48 is the page number. Three columns, each a run of labels with names beneath; Textract joined cells across columns into rows, so each name was assigned to the column whose sequence it continues. Single-person office labels (High School Principal, Assistant Principal, Administrative Secretary, Computer Coordinator, Director of Athletics) go in role_raw; department labels govern the names below them (grade_or_dept). The guidance grade ranges and 'Secretary' printed after a name are role_raw. Least certain placements: Amy Granato (line 46) sits in the middle cell of that row and is read as continuing Health under Julie Bertram and Shirley McGowan, not as Nurse; Ronald Lamothe (37) as Social Studies; Mark O'Malley (42) as Industrial Tech. Richard Stachowicz is printed twice (Physical Education and Director of Athletics); both kept."
